<title>USA: US July leading indicators +0.2 pct - Conference Bd.</title>
<headline>US July leading indicators +0.2 pct - Conference Bd.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Conference Board index of leading, coincident and lagging indicators (1987=100) and percent changes from previous months, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>    -			Index--July  June-Rev from   May</p>
<p> Leading Indicators    103.1   0.2    0.5   0.5     0.2</p>
<p> Coincident Indicators 121.1   0.1    0.3   0.5     0.5</p>
<p> Lagging Indicators    103.0   0.6   Unch  -0.1     0.2</p>
<p>Following are components of the index of leading indicators with net contributions to monthly changes.</p>
<p>    -			   July   June-Rev from   May</p>
<p> Average Workweek	  -0.13   0.09   0.04     0.09</p>
<p> Initial Jobless Claims   0.13  -0.01  -0.01     0.04</p>
<p> Consumer Goods Orders    0.08   0.01  -0.02     0.05</p>
<p> Slower Deliveries	 -0.08   0.11   0.11     0.03</p>
<p> Plant, Equipment Orders  0.07  -0.02  -0.04     0.07</p>
<p>    -			   July   June-Rev from   May</p>
<p> Building Permits	   0.04  -0.04  -0.04    -0.01</p>
<p> Unfilled Orders	   -0.02  -0.04  -0.04    -0.01</p>
<p> Materials Prices	   0.16   0.21   0.22     0.09</p>
<p> Stock Prices		-0.10   0.03   0.03     0.06</p>
<p> Money Supply		-0.02   0.07   0.08    -0.09</p>
<p> Consumer Expectations    0.04   0.09   0.09    -0.07</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast a 0.2 percent increase in July leading indicators.</p>
<p>The July advance marks the sixth consecutively monthly rise.</p>
</text>
